l","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}","name":"Unsummon","oracle_id":"837182db-1bf3-4a2c-bd01-1af9d9873561","oracle_text":"Return target creature to its owner's hand.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-04-24","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":3.0,"color_identity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{3}","name":"Veilstone Amulet","oracle_id":"55e21534-ec3e-46e1-8faf-59f0c3d48128","oracle_text":"Whenever you cast a spell, creatures you control can't be the targets of spells or abilities your opponents control this turn.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2007-05-04","toughness":null,"type_line":"Artifact"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["G"],"colors":["G"],"defense":null,"keywords":["Kicker"],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{G}","name":"Vines of Vastwood","oracle_id":"8998d211-5ca6-41d2-bc64-f51f70bd41e5","oracle_text":"Kicker {G} (You may pay an additional {G} as you cast this spell.)\nTarget creature can't be the target of spells or abilities your opponents control this turn. If this spell was kicked, that creature gets +4/+4 until end of turn.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2015-05-22","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":2.0,"color_identity":["R"],"colors":["R"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{R}{R}","name":"Reverberate","oracle_id":"a1f55890-31c5-4ed4-a2cd-7a4a9f05f8ca","oracle_text":"Copy target instant or sorcery spell. You may choose new targets for the copy.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2012-07-13","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it.","oracle_id":"a7e97fa9-4b72-4548-b854-5be5f18a6f1a","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not the same as hexproof. If, for example, you target one of your opponent's creatures, your opponents won't be able to target their own creature with spells or abilities.","oracle_id":"8998d211-5ca6-41d2-bc64-f51f70bd41e5","published_at":"2013-04-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a card or token enters as a copy of a permanent, the new permanent isn't kicked, even if the original was.","oracle_id":"8998d211-5ca6-41d2-bc64-f51f70bd41e5","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a spell's kicker cost was paid, the spell is \"kicked.\"","oracle_id":"8998d211-5ca6-41d2-bc64-f51f70bd41e5","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you copy a kicked spell on the stack, the copy is also kicked. If the copied spell is a permanent spell, the token the copy of that spell becomes when it enters is also kicked.","oracle_id":"8998d211-5ca6-41d2-bc64-f51f70bd41e5","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you put a permanent with a kicker ability onto the battlefield without casting it, you can't kick it.","oracle_id":"8998d211-5ca6-41d2-bc64-f51f70bd41e5","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The kicker ability doesn't let you pay a kicker cost more than once.","oracle_id":"8998d211-5ca6-41d2-bc64-f51f70bd41e5","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"To determine a spell's total cost, start with the mana cost (or an alternative cost if another card's effect allows you to pay one instead), add any cost increases (such as kicker), then apply any cost reductions. The spell's mana value remains unchanged, no matter what the total cost to cast it was.","oracle_id":"8998d211-5ca6-41d2-bc64-f51f70bd41e5","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the spell Reverberate copies has an X whose value was determined as it was cast (like Earthquake does), the copy has the same value of X.","oracle_id":"a1f55890-31c5-4ed4-a2cd-7a4a9f05f8ca","published_at":"2010-08-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The copy will have the same targets as the spell it's copying unless you choose new ones. You may change any number of the targets, including all of them or none of them. If, for one of the targets, you can't choose a new legal target, then it remains unchanged (even if the current target is illegal).","oracle_id":"a1f55890-31c5-4ed4-a2cd-7a4a9f05f8ca","published_at":"2010-08-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Reverberate can target (and copy) any instant or sorcery spell, not just one with targets. It doesn't matter who controls it.","oracle_id":"a1f55890-31c5-4ed4-a2cd-7a4a9f05f8ca","published_at":"2010-08-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"When Reverberate resolves, it creates a copy of a spell. You control the copy. That copy is created on the stack, so it's not \"cast.\" Abilities that trigger when a player casts a spell won't trigger. The copy will then resolve like a normal spell, after players get a chance to cast spells and activate abilities.","oracle_id":"a1f55890-31c5-4ed4-a2cd-7a4a9f05f8ca","published_at":"2010-08-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the copy says that it affects \"you,\" it affects the controller of the copy, not the controller of the original spell. Similarly, if the copy says that it affects an \"opponent,\" it affects an opponent of the copy's controller, not an opponent of the original spell's controller.","oracle_id":"a1f55890-31c5-4ed4-a2cd-7a4a9f05f8ca","published_at":"2010-08-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the spell Reverberate copies is modal (that is, it says \"Choose one —\" or the like), the copy will have the same mode. You can't choose a different one.","oracle_id":"a1f55890-31c5-4ed4-a2cd-7a4a9f05f8ca","published_at":"2010-08-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can't choose to pay any additional costs for the copy. However, effects based on any additional costs that were paid for the original spell are copied as though those same costs were paid for the copy too. For example, if a player sacrifices a 3/3 creature to cast Fling, and you copy it with Reverberate, the copy of Fling will also deal 3 damage to its target.","oracle_id":"a1f55890-31c5-4ed4-a2cd-7a4a9f05f8ca","published_at":"2010-08-15","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
